\section*{Numerical semiampleness of Kähler adjoints}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
On the stated compact Kähler pairs, a nef adjoint with an additional nef rational line is claimed to have a semiample representative of its Bott--Chern class, allowing a flat change of bundle. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Let $X$ be smooth connected compact Kähler, $B\ge0$ rational simple-normal-crossing with coefficients below one, and $M\in\operatorname{Pic}(X)\otimes\mathbb Q$. Assume pseudo-effectivity of $K_X+B$, and nefness of both $M$ and $D=K_X+B+M$, OpenAI claims
\[
\exists\text{ semiample rational line bundle }L:\quad c_1(L)=c_1(D)\text{ in }H^{1,1}_{\mathrm{BC}}(X,\mathbb R).
\]
Nef means the Chern class lies in the closed Kähler cone; pseudo-effective means it contains a positive current. Semiampleness means an actual positive integral multiple is globally generated. Equality is of Bott--Chern classes, not of line bundles.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 036, 2026-10-04): The induction uses projective positive-part results when algebraic reduction has positive-dimensional image. In algebraic dimension zero, decomposition into torus and generically symplectic pieces, extension estimates, and compact cycle spaces provide the numerical representative while preserving the distinction from an actual line identity.

